WEBVTT

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:43.820
Do you think that the Z will forgive me?
That time I couldn't save it.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:48.880
Let me take you to the Z.
See it with your own eyes.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.640
<i>That guy...</i>

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.900
<i>That guy is...!</i>

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:59.600
<i>The driver of the legendary Devil Z!</i>

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.580
<i>I didn't get to save you...</i>

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:10.470
<i>but we must race together again.</i>

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:14.980
<i>It's my turn this time... I'm gonna rebuild you.</i>

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:21.440
<i>Reviving the Demon</i>

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.380
You sure you don't mind me borrowing this?

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.990
No, just don't tell my boss.

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:30.320
I can sort you out the money for petrol.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:33.000
You gonna be able to repair that body?

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.510
I'm going to take it to a body work expert.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:42.140
A decade ago, he made the Devil Z able to withstand 300km/h.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.400
This guy is still around?

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:49.400
Yeah, he's a body work genius. He's an iron and aluminum genius.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.010
Here?

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:56.660
Yeah... don't you bring your cars here too?

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:59.560
No, we don't bring them here anymore.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.150
How come?

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.870
Our car range is a little wide for this place.

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:08.130
It's been a long time, Kitami-san!

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.910
You got a car body for us to repair?

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:13.130
Yeah. I think you're gonna be the only one who can help me.

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:18.630
<i>Impossible... there's no way they'll get it back to how it looked.</i>

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.890
If you could just do the favor once again...

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:28.380
It's got this bad all over again?

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.390
Ok, ok... no problem.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.850
We've got a great team of workers here.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:37.100
Plus, we've just imported a framework
repair machine from Germany.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.490
Good workers? Machine from Germany?

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.900
What are you talking about?

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.100
Huh?

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.430
I want you to do it.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.830
Use your block and hammer to take the dents out.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:50.190
Fuse the broken parts together again.

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.420
I need you to do it all by yourself.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.460
You gotta be joking. I can't do that anymore...

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:57.880
I need it done within a month.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:58.880
What?

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.880
And this time the body must be able to take 330km/h.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:03.590
330km/h?

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:08.760
I need this body stronger yet more refined than any other car.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.360
Only you can repair the Devil Z.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:12.870
Devil?

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.350
This is...

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:20.360
Yeah, that's right. Please take care
of it. You're the best at what you do.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.110
The Devil Z...

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.720
<i>It's still alive...</i>

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.910
<i>No way... I can't do this anymore.</i>

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:42.640
<i>This man...</i>

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:49.250
<i>Is he the one that stole your heart?</i>

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:54.880
<i>Can he... can he drive you?</i>

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:59.000
Are you Takagi-san?

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.370
Kitami-san said I'd find you here...

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.610
and that you were looking after the Z.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:07.200
He said that you'd have no problem with me taking it.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:10.040
What do you plan to do with it?

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:13.570
It's not worth much really... not even for donor parts.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:15.890
I wanna repair it.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:17.530
That's not possible.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:24.890
You don't look very professional, you
might be able to repair the looks a bit.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:28.350
A body this bad won't last much longer.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:33.950
Just like this paper box.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:36.380
Once it has been crushed...

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:40.470
even if you repair it, it'll never be as strong again.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.040
It doesn't matter.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:42.980
Doesn't matter?

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:46.040
Even if it'll never run again.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:48.730
I still want to try and repair the Z.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:52.120
<i>Why does he have that look in his eyes?</i>

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:08.710
We've finally got the speed up to 300.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:11.700
Yeah, but boost of 1.5,

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.920
it is rather risky.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.130
It takes too long to get from 250 to 300km/h.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:19.190
It's losing too much power.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:20.940
Anyway, a boost of 1.2...

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.430
What is it, Hiramoto?

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.090
There's a car catching up to us really fast from behind.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.760
31... Z31?

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:29.940
Z31?

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:34.490
<i>There's a Z31 that overtook me easily
while I was cruising at 260km/h.</i>

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:35.950
<i>Harada?</i>

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:39.920
<i>Is it Harada?</i>

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:44.900
<i>Hiramoto-san.</i>

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:50.380
<i>Can you keep up with me?</i>

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.850
<i>Now way! Is that a VG engine?</i>

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:08.060
I see you've done some tuning, big time.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.260
I always see you cruising on Wangan.

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.860
A decent car far exceeds common sense...

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:17.120
It's amazing. He still tunes that car even
though he knows it's doing it no good.

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.040
I couldn't do it.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.590
That's why I've chosen an R to work on.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:22.870
He's got more faith in it than me.

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:27.320
He likes that Z31 a lot.

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:30.210
That's why he hangs on to it.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:33.880
You prefer the GT-R though, yeah?

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.790
You used to tell me...

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:40.390
that the top speed is gone within a seconds hesitation.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:44.890
You've gotta really like a car to trust it with your life.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:49.650
You've just started tuning it.
There's no time to get upset, Hiramoto.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:50.890
Yeah.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:03.290
<i>Are you gonna repair that thing all by yourself?</i>

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.170
<i>Yes.</i>

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:09.140
<i>Ok, then. You can use my place if you like.</i>

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:22.640
<i>Started this way of life at 15. Racing with a
car tuned by someone else for three years.</i>

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:28.650
<i>You idiot! How many times do I have to tell you?!</i>

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:31.000
<i>Iron and aluminum are alive.</i>

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.690
<i>They are breathing, like our skin.</i>

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:37.710
<i>You need to learn to get inside it and communicate with it.</i>

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:40.090
<i>What does the dented iron needs?</i>

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:42.460
<i>How are you gonna repair twisted aluminum?</i>

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.300
<i>Hammer it, stretch it, strengthen it...</i>

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:46.720
<i>You need to know how the iron feels.</i>

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:48.390
<i>What the aluminum is thinking...</i>

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:52.490
<i>Keep working on it, boy.</i>

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:54.430
<i>You'll get to know what it's all about.</i>

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:10.520
You bought an R, right?

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.000
I was surprised.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.470
I saw a great older car.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:15.870
What series is it?

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:19.700
TD06. The engine is a crank and casket job.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.050
What about the engine control unit?

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:22.370
No, it's just normal.

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:25.590
The burnout setting is F-CON.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:29.080
Typical Hiramoto-san...

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:33.340
Harada... your Z31 is tuned really well.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:36.090
You must have spent a lot of time on it.

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:37.570
Yeah, not anymore.

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:40.630
You should be careful.
You were really giving it some the other day.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:44.040
On Wangan, never underestimate the speed.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:46.140
It can turn its back on you at any time.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:58.670
Front fender, parts 4100-3 and 4.

00:09:58.670 --> 00:10:02.720
Front wheels use Bush rockers and shocks.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:09.120
You'll never restore it, even if you had
all the original manufacturers parts.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.870
I just wanna get it working again.

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:15.440
And then you start tuning it again?
That's a long term plan.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.300
That could take you up to 10 years to do it.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.950
It doesn't matter.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:22.350
Doesn't matter? So nothing is wrong then, huh?

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:30.650
That time, I wasn't able to save the Z.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.660
But I won't simply give up on it.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:36.020
I'll stick with it until it's done.

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:37.320
That's what I used to say to it...

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:43.280
I can spend my lifetime on it... I just wanna get it working again.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.990
<i>I needed it done within a month.</i>

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.610
<i>And this time the body must be able to take 330km/h.</i>

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:29.760
<i>Only you can repair the Devil Z.</i>

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:39.040
I'm leaving.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.240
What's the matter?

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:41.630
Hey, boss-san...?

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:48.350
Huh?

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.210
Takagi-san...

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:01.970
Yo!

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:07.220
Boss, the dark blue BMW...

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:09.500
Why are you in a uniform?

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.990
Fukuta, how long have you worked for me?

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:14.150
8 years.

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:15.870
It's been that long, huh?

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:19.580
Starting today, I'm not going to the office for a month.
You're in charge, ok?

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:20.590
Huh?

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:23.750
I made this Z, 10 years ago.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:28.520
With 600hp and a body that can take 300km/h.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:31.820
Not just a sports car but a proper race car.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:34.820
But not just to make the chassis stronger...

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:40.030
it must look good too. Iron and aluminum breathe just like us.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:44.040
I managed to do it, 10 years ago.

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:46.020
If I want to do it again, it has to be now.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:49.040
Only I can repair the Devil Z now.

00:12:50.570 --> 00:12:55.470
<i>The look in your eyes... gives me the strength to do it.</i>

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:57.540
<i>I'm sure that I can do it.</i>

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:14.010
How's it running now?

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:20.520
I managed to get it to 320 but it's
still a little weak around 280km/h.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.660
Ok, I'll tune it some more.

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:24.560
Anything else?

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:26.690
The rest is ok.

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:28.940
Then this'll be the last time.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:32.080
Over the next weeks, I want to get into the fine tuning.

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:34.590
I get it, Kitami-san.

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:38.580
Boss... boss?

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:42.080
What? Is it morning already?

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:46.160
Did you sleep here again?

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.070
Did you work all through the night again?

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:49.920
You should take care of yourself.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:52.560
I'll be fine, don't worry.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:57.930
<i>Another 15 days...</i>

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:05.610
Ok, well done.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:06.820
It's looking good.

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:13.320
The weld spot between the sheets of
iron is called a strengthening point.

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:17.160
There should be at least 200 on a normal race car.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:19.240
But of course, the more, the better.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:22.270
Did it have a fracture before?

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:23.350
Fracture?

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:24.290
No.

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:27.090
It's hard for fractured parts to break again.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:30.540
The fractured parts tend to become stronger.

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:38.880
You can't just add more welds or
frames to make the chassis stronger.

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:40.980
You need strengthening points to absorb any collision.

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:45.570
Only then could it withstand 300km/h.

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:50.620
Matsu, are you here?

00:14:51.270 --> 00:14:53.080
He's just gone out on a delivery.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:55.750
Oh, I'll come back later.

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:02.170
You should stop coming over looking for my boy.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:07.300
He's finally got himself a proper job,

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:09.640
but ever since you turned up...

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:17.140
You just wanna use people, don't you?

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:20.100
Please stop coming here.

00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:23.710
I understand.

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:36.150
No, this is not right...

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:43.620
I can't do it, I'm not the guy I was 10 years ago!

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:46.220
Dammit, dammit!

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:59.720
<i>How are you, Tatsuya?</i>

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:01.740
<i>I'm doing fine here.</i>

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:05.080
<i>It's been a month since I left Japan.</i>

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:08.480
<i>I've got used to life in England.</i>

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:12.240
<i>It's important not to mix with the wrong crowd.</i>

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:15.000
<i>Everyone seems so happy here.</i>

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:19.720
<i>Akio, who worked every day on the Z...</i>

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:23.900
<i>Tatsuya, who would show me the sunrise over the Wangan...</i>

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:32.750
<i>I try to forget about my brother Akio and the Devil Z.</i>

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:36.540
<i>You should forget about it too, Tatsuya.</i>

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:39.320
<i>Just get on with it.</i>

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:42.520
<i>I can't do it.</i>

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:50.450
<i>I can't do it anymore. I've gotta keep going until I reach the end.</i>

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:04.600
<i>The baby was born on 18th June.</i>

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:08.500
<i>He weighs 3,24kg.</i>

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:12.640
<i>I can't live with you anymore!</i>

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:19.870
<i>I'm a coward, so... I can't live with you anymore!</i>

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:37.270
Damn, it's not working.

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:45.460
I've finally found you.
Kitami-san wouldn't tel me where you were.

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:51.920
Huh, Takagi-san?

00:17:57.030 --> 00:17:57.980
Akio-kun!

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:02.990
Takagi-san! Takagi-san!

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:05.030
Hang in there, Takagi-san!

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:12.240
Basically he's been overworking himself...

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:14.660
He has taken on an awful lot of stress.

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.480
Plus, he has quite a weak heart.

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:21.090
I mean, he wasn't that healthy before this happened.

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:24.540
I'm pretty sure he suffers with high blood-pressure too.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.650
<i>Akio, forgive me.</i>

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:38.460
<i>I'm just not gonna get it done.</i>

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:51.300
I called the body shop. They said you'd been rushed to the hospital.

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:54.690
You should get your rest tonight.
Tomorrow, you've got a lot of work to do.

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:56.430
Another 10 days...

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:59.740
I can't do it anymore.

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:03.870
I don't even think I'll be able to repair it again!

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:08.450
You're still a crybaby, just like you always were.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:12.750
Remember that second Porsche Turbo at Green Auto?

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:16.090
It had a 280km/h crash and was a complete write-off.

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:19.360
Even the older guys said it was a lost cause.

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:20.580
But not you...

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:24.090
<i>Let me do it! There is no body I can not fix!</i>

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:29.920
We never thought a crybaby like you would say something like that.

00:19:30.910 --> 00:19:33.060
But you still did it that time.

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:36.390
Right? Just think about it.

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:39.550
The midnight blue Devil's body...

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:42.990
Starts to move slowly.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:46.050
Revved up 9000rpm and then into second gear.

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:48.910
Accelerate it hard and into third gear...

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.130
Fourth gear...

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:53.750
The tires are gripping the ground really well...

00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:56.550
The way ahead is nice and clear.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:58.880
Now, you go into fifth...

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:05.140
250, 260... nothing but fresh air in front of you.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:08.090
270, 280...

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:13.890
An L28 with a twin turbo. My newly
tuned Devil won't stop accelerating.

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:18.390
The engine... it still wants do accelerate.

00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:23.340
Now, it's in your hands. Have faith. You're the bodywork genius.

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:39.030
<i>Everything is done now.</i>

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:42.390
<i>Even the smallest details have now been modified.</i>

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:44.380
<i>It's now become the most powerful engine.</i>

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:45.280
<i>But...</i>

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:50.400
<i>But something... is still missing.</i>

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:54.120
Matsu?

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:04.830
Did my mother say something to you?

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:06.860
Damn that old woman...

00:21:07.340 --> 00:21:09.590
Speaking of which, that new exhaust is ready.

00:21:10.310 --> 00:21:13.640
Matsu, that's enough, don't worry about the exhaust...

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:19.620
Listen... an exhaust made by some
average guy isn't good enough for this car.

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:20.590
It'll lose horsepower.

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:23.020
How so? Which part isn't working properly?

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:23.850
The whole thing.

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:28.350
What I need is an advanced exhaust
system that can "up" the horsepower.

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:32.040
That's why I can't use bent pipe built by average mechanics.

00:21:35.050 --> 00:21:38.680
Using people, huh?

00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:42.030
Your mother is rather sharp-tongued.

00:21:42.850 --> 00:21:46.830
That's right! I just used you for parts!

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:49.990
That's enough, Hiramoto. That's enough..

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:52.290
See ya.

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:56.020
I'll just leave this here anyway.

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:58.120
You can dump it if you don't want it.

00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:01.870
I'm still your friend anyway. I'm fine with it.

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:06.590
But I thought you'd appreciate the exhaust I'd made you.

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:14.480
<i>I do appreciate it.</i>

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:22.060
<i>Matsu... how on earth did you make an exhaust this good?</i>

00:22:23.370 --> 00:22:26.040
<i>This is it. This is the best, Matsu.</i>

00:22:26.040 --> 00:22:32.160
<i>It's what I needed. The best exhaust
system combined with the best engine.</i>

00:22:32.640 --> 00:22:35.720
<i>Yes, this is becoming the most powerful GT-R!</i>

00:22:39.560 --> 00:22:42.160
Have you been working all night?

00:22:44.450 --> 00:22:45.120
Yeah.

00:22:45.450 --> 00:22:47.680
Do you plan to do this all by yourself?

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:50.710
I made a promise.

00:22:50.710 --> 00:22:52.710
Excuse me, Akio but that's impossible.

00:22:53.940 --> 00:22:56.900
From now on, it'll have to be me that finishes it.

00:22:57.240 --> 00:22:58.390
Takagi-san?

00:22:58.740 --> 00:23:01.400
I have accepted this task.

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:06.900
Only I can make it even stronger than it was before.

00:23:09.070 --> 00:23:11.150
Come and get it in ten days.

00:23:11.150 --> 00:23:13.660
The Devil Z will be revived by then.
